            <div xml:id="d9">

                <pb facs="0113" n="17" xml:id="pg17"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3731/198: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Crowder</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Paraphrase]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1926-05-17T16:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">May 17, 1926—4
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 8:35 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>84. From a source close to President Machado I have received the following
                    reliable information: <list>
                        <label>(1)</label>
                        <item>That President Machado sent the note transmitted with my despatch No.
                            1416, May 7, out of deference to an almost unanimous public opinion in
                            Cuba on the matter;</item>
                        <label>(2)</label>
                        <item>That the Government of Cuba would appreciate as an act of courtesy
                            Department’s prompt expression, in most general terms, of its
                            willingness, when a convenient time may offer itself, to enter upon a
                            discussion of trade relations between the United States and Cuba with
                            view to render them truly reciprocal, even though such discussion should
                            lead to no result;</item>
                        <label>(3)</label>
                        <item>That Department’s unwillingness to enter into such a discussion as
                            suggested above would seriously impair prestige of the present
                            administration.</item>
                    </list></p>
                <p>I have expressed no opinion as to what Department’s decision might be.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Crowder</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
